  "description": "The tie-break of the closure is the order of the breadth-first walk itself, not the least slug sequence. a requires d, b requires c, c and d both require e; the selection is a and b. The walk expands the selection in slug order (a then b, adding d and c), then the next frontier in slug order (c before d), so e is first reached from c and records the path b → c → e. Both paths to e have length 2; the lexicographically least slug sequence would be a → d → e, which this case refuses. Expected values derived by hand from AGSC-07-04 as amended for 1.0.0.",
